{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1086565-starting-up-the-giovanni-chronicles","id":1086565,"title":"Starting up The Giovanni Chronicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-02T05:36:58-07:00","id":1086565,"title":"Starting up The Giovanni Chronicles","content":"So, it begins!<br /> In a fit of inspiration I asked my gaming friends if they wanted to join in to a Dark Ages Vampire chronicle and it seem like I have to start figuring out my game now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have asked my players to focus on the individual first, adding thoughts about clan to the finished person in the end, as I'm trying/going for more of a story/rp less cool discipline murder mayhem game.<br /> <br /> The characters so far:<br /> <br /> An ambitious woman in her 30's, wife of Piero di Cosimo de' Medici, a very influential noble merchant from Italy. Ending up as Lasombra.<br /> <br /> A beautiful yong woman in her early 20's, the spoiled brat, younger sister of Piero di Cosimo de' Medici. Ending up as Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> A stonemason/architect from england seeking purpose and work, heading to Italy. Clan to be decided.<br /> <br /> A Italian/Arabic monk/physician seeking to better the world after loosing his mentor to disease. Chose Healer Salubri<br /> <br /> And finally a veteran crusader, wanting to be Warrior Salubri.<br /> <br /> <br /> So what do you think about the clan/bloodline setup?<br /> <br /> I really do want to let everyone go any clan/bloodline they want but breaking the story would be a bit sad tho.<br /> <br /> Do you think a game with dual Salubri would be manageable? The Tremere issue here will be rather prominent <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, the player creating the stonemason hinted about True Brujah, and I don't really know how to do about that. The rarest of the rare, rather alient in mindset. Do you allow/hate/love/encourage the bloodline?<br /> <br /> Finally. Three bloodlines in one Chronicle? They should be rather rare at like 6% for all vampires in official resources.<br /> <br /> Please feel free to give me some input or advice!<br /> <br /> My Very Best Regards<br /> Anafear","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13284-anafear","name":"Anafear","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:48:43-07:00","id":1086630,"title":"","content":"Congrats! I am currently playing in a Giovanni Chronicles game where we didn't pick clans, plus our ST switched the NPCs around, and added new ones for different clans. I love the story! Good luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>For different game play videos of White Wolf Games from my play group<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBU...IhwsM3kHK56SRA</a><br /> <a href=\"https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night\" target=\"_blank\">https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night</a><br /> If you want to find White Wolf game play media or subject matter media<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/groups/862703457198327/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11618-christopherzacher","name":"ChristopherZacher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"631"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T10:29:50-07:00","id":1087217,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">The stonemason is now doomed to become Tzimisce.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I have been thinking since I posted and got some input and now have a outline of how to handle the Salubri situation.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I'll rework the Tremere in Giovannis company a bit. I am leaning to a failed/uncomplete/tainted vampire who is Tremere in all aspects but the tainted blood, retaining qualities from Salubri victims, maninfesting amongst other things the third eye and some unwanted Valeren.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Naturally the Tremere will go to all lenghts to make sure these features do not reach other members of the clan, and as of such do not intemingle with them any more than nessecary.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Seeking another power base in the company of the influential Giovanni is the solution at the moment.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I don't really feel I need to change the interactions with said Tremere very much other than this.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I hope it will turn out nicely, my players usually gobble down whatever I feed them.</span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13284-anafear","name":"Anafear","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T15:35:20-07:00","id":1087361,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'm always a little hesitant when a bunch of players want to run Bloodlines mostly out of concern that they just want a Bloodline's special power. I always try ask the players if their concept truly requires the Bloodline they want and/or what they want to get out of their character being that of certain Bloodline. Sometimes they do have a solid concept and reasoning and I give it the okay. Other times, no so much and we discuss where to go from there.<br /> <br /> If you're okay with having two of the players as Salubri or you think they are up to it as I just said, go for it. If you're having doubts about them, maybe you should sit down and discuss it with the players.<br /> <br /> I love the Giovanni Chronicles and have played it before. We didn't finish the entire run but we play pretty far. Like Chris here said, we ran it where we players didn't have control over our Clans, building straight up mortals and then over the course of the Last Supper, converting them into vampires. And that I think is the best way to run the GC, focusing on the human they were first and foremost. It led to some amusing and interesting things in our game. <br /> <br /> One player created a young noblewoman that a deeply devoted Christian and was preparing to become a nun when she was invited to the party. As it turned out, she was the preferred meal and later Childe of the Settie of the Conspiracy which in turn led to some very interesting things with her character. She just ran with the concept and having been faced with becoming a vampire, especially a Settite. After the events of the Last Supper she went on a long period of penitence and flagellation over her existence that lasted for better part of her first century. At that point several things happened. The first was the realization that she had now existed beyond her natural lifespan and that began to tear her apart inside, leaving her wondering why God would let such good and pious person as her be damned as a vampire. Not long after that she had her first real encounter with her Clan in the form of a trio of Settites in Venice. Long story short, it did not go well for anyone involved. Two of the three Settites died and their haven looted and then burned down. By the start of second book, she was in control of nunnery outside of Venice, ghouling the senior nuns there, pouring over scripture, mortal and Cainite lore, and pretty much anything else she could get her hands in a bid to find some purpose in her damnation.<br /> <br /> After the events in that book, she started develop down a path towards a path that, well as she (the player) told me due to the game coming to a premature end, turning the nunnery completely into her cult, embracing several Childer and moving to Milan, cultivating ties to the Sabbat. Her end goal was to have the character become the head of a Settite Antitribu group separate from the Serpents of Light. She had talking about combining aspects of the Catholic Faith, Sabbat practices, Settite beliefs, Noddist lore, and things from VtR's Lancea Sanctum into her brood's beliefs and practices.<br /> <br /> Which would have been very interesting to see the final product of all that in the Modern Nights.<br /> <br /> Of course she was one of our groups most veteran VtM players so if anyone could have pulled that off it was her.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}